    turnFlow: '1. Fishing: Match a card from hand to one on the table (for number cards you may also capture a chosen sum-equal combination).\n2. Face Cards: J/Q/K capture exactly one matching face card and cannot be used in sum captures or declarations.\n3. Declarations (Builds): Create plain or group declarations from number cards. A player making or raising a declaration must hold a matching card for later capture.\n4. Raising and ownership: Opponents may raise plain declarations; group declarations cannot be raised. The player who most recently created/added to a declaration is responsible for capturing it.\n5. Xeri: Capturing all table cards in one play scores 10 points (with standard exceptions for the opening table-clear and some end-of-round cases).\n6. Further deals: When hands are exhausted, dealer gives 6 new cards each from stock; no new table cards are dealt.',
